    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0573" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">638.5131/142: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-29T13:00:00-05:00">April 29, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. My despatches 453 of March 24, and 465 of April 7.<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d567-f1"/> The Foreign Minister informed me today that exchange of
                        notes<anchor n="62" xml:id="d567-f2"/> effecting <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi</hi> pending consummation of Franco-Haitian commercial treaty
                    negotiations had just been signed. The <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi> gives Haiti a quota of approximately 37,000 sacks of coffee to
                    be shipped from here between now and September 1; the French get straight
                    minimum tariff treatment and there is no mention of an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >avenant</hi> or of specific tariff reductions for additional non-specialty
                    articles.</p>
                <p>Amplifying despatch by air mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gordon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
